      "text": "To evaluate \\(\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor\\), we need to determine the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\).\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of \\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\):\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{3} \\approx -1.6667\n\\]\n\nThe floor function \\(\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor\\) gives the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(x\\). For \\(x = -1.6667\\), the greatest integer less than or equal to \\(-1.6667\\) is \\(-2\\).\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor -\\frac{5}{3} \\right\\rfloor = -2\n\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-2}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Calculate the value of -5/3\nvalue = -5 / 3\n\n# Use the floor function to find the greatest integer less than or equal to -5/3\nfloor_value = math.floor(value)\nprint(floor_value)\n```",
